-`make up` derives root-only Compose secret files under ignored `deploy/secrets/`; no secret is baked
-into an image. It installs eight LaunchAgents in `~/Library/LaunchAgents`:
+`make up LEVEL=voice|durable|full` derives root-only Compose secret files under ignored
+`deploy/secrets/`; no secret is baked into an image. The first `make start LEVEL=...` installs the
+host runtime and then selects which LaunchAgents remain loaded:
+
+- `voice`: inference broker and Pi Voice Service;
+- `durable`: voice services plus Pi Durable Owner, with task execution on the host;
+- `full`: all host services, including Gondolin task execution and image building.
+
+All levels share the core Compose services required by the voice edge and gateway. The `full`
+Compose profile additionally runs Gitea, its ingress, and the trace-render worker. During initial
+host installation, `make start` temporarily starts Gitea because repository synchronization uses
+it; lower levels stop the profile services after installation. The persistent Pi Voice sandbox
+still uses Gondolin and clones its workspace from Gitea when it starts.
+Thus durable mode avoids Gondolin for durable tasks, while the separate Pi Voice
+sandbox continues to use its existing Gondolin runtime.
+
+The host services installed for `full` are:
 
 - inference broker: local Parakeet v3 MLX, Ollama, and Kokoro capability on `127.0.0.1:9443`;
 - music generation: ACE-Step audio and language models on `127.0.0.1:8001`;
