diff --git a/products/voice-agent/README.md b/products/voice-agent/README.md
index e275f77..ae3b512 100644
--- a/products/voice-agent/README.md
+++ b/products/voice-agent/README.md
@@ -101,13 +101,28 @@ tools still execute through Gondolin rather than in the voice stack.
 
 ## Start
 
+Choose a runtime level with `LEVEL=voice`, `LEVEL=durable`, or `LEVEL=full`;
+the default is `full`. Voice runs the broker and Pi Voice LaunchAgents with the
+core Compose services. Durable adds Pi Durable Owner and selects host task
+execution. Full adds the remaining LaunchAgents, Gondolin task execution, Gitea
+and trace rendering. Switching levels stops host agents and optional containers
+outside the selected level. Initial host-service installation still prepares
+the complete runtime; the selector controls what stays running.
+
+Voice and durable use the same core Compose services; their difference is the
+host LaunchAgent set and Pi Durable execution mode. Durable avoids Gondolin for
+durable tasks. The persistent Pi Voice Service still uses its own Gondolin
+sandbox, and its workspace is cloned from Gitea during service startup. The
+installer starts Gitea temporarily for that setup, then voice and durable stop
+the Gitea and trace-render Compose profile.
+
 ```bash
 cd products/voice-agent
 make setup
 # Configure deploy/.env and the service files under deploy/host-env.
 make pull-model
 make host-preflight
-make start
+make start LEVEL=voice
 make login
 make warm-models
 ```
@@ -157,12 +172,12 @@ name when the Mac itself is not connected as a Tailscale client.
 
 ```bash
 make status       # Compose services, tailnet state, native service state
-make start        # deploy, verify, and return after services become healthy
-make up           # deploy, verify, and follow service stdout
-make native-status # inspect all eight launchd services
-make native-start  # start the installed native services; Compose dependencies must be running
-make native-stop   # unload the native services in reverse order
-make native-restart # restart the native services and wait for model readiness
+make start LEVEL=voice    # choose voice, durable, or full
+make up LEVEL=durable     # deploy a level and follow service stdout
+make native-status        # inspect all installed LaunchAgents
+make native-start LEVEL=durable # activate only that level's host services
+make native-stop          # unload every installed host service
+make native-restart LEVEL=full # restart the selected host services
 make logs         # follow container and native-service stdout
 make verify       # isolation, capabilities, ingress, broker, and gateway checks
 make grafana-password # print the local Grafana credential after make up
@@ -182,8 +197,12 @@ make down         # stop native and Compose services; preserve data volumes
 make check        # tests, lint, type checks, build, Compose and plist validation
 ```
 
-`make start` installs and starts the native services after S3Mock and Gitea are healthy.
-Use `make native-start` after installation when those container dependencies are already running.
+`make start LEVEL=...` prepares the deployment, installs host services after S3Mock and Gitea are
+available, then leaves only the selected level running. Durable selects
+`WORKER_PI_EXECUTION_MODE=host`; full selects Gondolin task execution. Gitea is
+available only at full level after startup. `make native-start LEVEL=...` switches an already
+installed host-service set without rebuilding it; use `make start LEVEL=...` to switch the whole
+deployment.
 `make native-stop` unloads the services, so launchd will not immediately restart jobs configured
 with `KeepAlive`. `make down` stops native services before stopping Compose. `make native-status`
 reads launchd state without changing it; `make verify` checks service readiness.
